WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.760
<b>The Fourth</b>

38
00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.110
Waa! My hat! Where's my hat?!

39
00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.030
It's right there, calm down.

40
00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.400
Oh good, here it is.

41
00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.940
Have a good nap?

42
00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.700
Hey... Those pirates...

43
00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.870
They're gone now,
all thanks to you.

44
00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:17.950
Me?

45
00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:22.710
Yeah, and Ghin asked me to tell you
that he said, "See you on the Grand Line."

46
00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.210
Huh, he did?

47
00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.330
To you?

48
00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.840
No, to you!

49
00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.590
So, I guess I don't have to
do anymore lame-o chores,

50
00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:35.890
since I got those pirates
off your back, right?

51
00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:37.140
That's the deal.

52
00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.510
Hey, I was wondering...

53
00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:41.640
No, I'm not gonna run away
with you to become a pirate.

54
00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:42.430
Aw...

55
00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.560
I've got some unfinished business here.

56
00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.110
I'll stay until Zeff
acknowledges my skill.

57
00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:50.070
Okay then, I give up.

58
00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:51.860
That means you let go!

59
00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.370
I can't just leave...

60
00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:01.620
These bozos don't know the first
thing about how to run a restaurant.

61
00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:05.040
But still, I promised myself
that one of these days...

62
00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.830
I'll go to the Grand Line.

63
00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:11.050
Well, let's go right now!

64
00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:13.260
It just isn't the right time. Not yet.

65
00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:17.970
There is one place.

66
00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:20.260
Say, have you ever
heard of the All Blue?

67
00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.100
Nuh-uh.

68
00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.180
You've got to be kidding me!

69
00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.850
That sea is a miracle.

70
00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:30.150
In the All Blue, there are fish
from the East Blue, the West Blue,

71
00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.150
the North Blue, and the South Blue.

72
00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:35.320
That one stretch of ocean has it all!

73
00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:36.360
Hmph.

74
00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:39.240
To us cooks, it's a
culinary dream come true.

75
00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.200
A place that fantastic has got to be
on the Grand Line somewhere, right?

76
00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.750
I mean, where else...

77
00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:51.460
The little brat looks truly happy.

78
00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.670
Heh. What an idiot.

79
00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:02.310
Alright, guys! Soup's on!

80
00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:07.100
<b>Employee Dining Room
2nd Floor, Baratie</b>

81
00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:13.020
Really?

82
00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.400
Oh good, they saved us some seats.

83
00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.490
They did?

84
00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:18.450
No chairs left for you.

85
00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:21.120
Just sit on the floor and eat!

86
00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.620
There are no chairs?

87
00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.700
That doesn't seem right.

88
00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.410
This is a restaurant.

89
00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.250
All right, fine.

90
00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.580
They sure are acting strange.

91
00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.090
Well, that's nothing new.

92
00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:36.590
Bunch of jerks.

93
00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:38.170
Hey! What is this?

94
00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:40.130
Who prepared the soup this morning?!

95
00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.640
Oh! I did!

96
00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.300
This stuff is pretty good, huh?

97
00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.220
I think I really out did myself!

98
00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.220
Is that a joke?!

99
00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:50.690
I can barely hold this
slop down! Bleh! Bleh!

100
00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.860
I thought someone
like you, would like slop.

101
00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:01.570
It makes sense to me, seeing
as, that's what pigs like.

102
00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:05.740
Ha! Just face it Sanji, your
soup sucks. It's disgusting!

103
00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:07.910
Bleh, bleh, bleh!

104
00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:10.960
That soup is nothing
short of a delicacy.

105
00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.750
There's something wrong
with your taste buds!

106
00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:21.760
Ugh! That's gross!

107
00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:24.100
I can't eat this!

108
00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.560
Bleh, bleh! Revolting!

109
00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.180
This soup is horrible!

110
00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:38.900
What the hell's going
on, you bastards?!

111
00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.900
We're sick of the way you run things!

112
00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.740
You're a sham of a Sous Chef
and everybody knows it!

113
00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.490
You can't just settle every single
little disagreement with violence!

114
00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:49.870
If the food's bad,
then we're gonna say so!

115
00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.750
What'd you say?!

116
00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:57.630
Boss!

117
00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:59.050
Geezer!

118
00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:04.510
That wretched little dish
tasted like stewed garbage.

119
00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:09.520
If we ever served that kind of trash
here, we'd go out of business!

120
00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.060
Are you really this stupid?!

121
00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:14.690
Just how is my soup any different
from the stuff you make? How?!

122
00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:16.770
You think they're the same?

123
00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:22.650
Don't flatter yourself!

124
00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:25.360
The Boss punched him!

125
00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:26.990
He didn't kick him!

126
00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:30.240
You think you can lecture me
on the art of cooking, do ya?

127
00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.120
Fat chance!

128
00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:35.580
I'm a man who has cooked on more seas
than days that you've been alive!

129
00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:41.130
Damn it!

130
00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:52.850
Gah! What's all the fuss about?

131
00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:55.020
This soup's totally awesome!

132
00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:56.650
All of us know the soup is good.

133
00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:57.270
Huh?

134
00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:59.690
I know he's an outstanding chef.

135
00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:02.110
Everyone here on the Baratie does.

136
00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.570
Yeah, he's great.

137
00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:06.240
Aside from Chef Zeff,
he's the best we got.

138
00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:07.990
That was scary wasn't it?

139
00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:09.740
He seriously snapped.

140
00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:10.990
Yeah...

141
00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:21.500
But that thick-skulled idiot wouldn't
listen to us if we tried to reason with him.

142
00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:24.970
Hey, listen.

143
00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:26.050
Hm?

144
00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:29.680
You were saying that you needed
a cook for your ship, right?

145
00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:32.680
Well, this isn't something I
want to be asking anyone,

146
00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:36.850
but... would you mind taking
that little brat along with you?

147
00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:38.730
Take him to the Grand Line.

148
00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:40.020
Hm?

149
00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.230
That would be best for him.

150
00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:44.900
The Grand Line is his dream.

151
00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:49.780
Geez, Boss, you sure made
us put on a hell of a show.

152
00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:53.910
Oh man, I was worried he was gonna
figure it out 'cause of your bad acting!

153
00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:57.710
C'mon, your acting was
way worse than mine!

154
00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.380
I'm gonna get
some more of that soup!

155
00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:01.750
Yeah, that stuff is good!

156
00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:19.650
I can hear everything, Dumbasses.

157
00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.650
So, what do you say, Kid?

158
00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:24.610
No way.

159
00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:31.200
But earlier, you mentioned you
needed a cook for your ship.

160
00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.700
Just what are you trying to say?

161
00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.620
That he's suddenly not
good enough for ya'?

162
00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:36.750
Oh, he's good.

163
00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:40.500
And I'd love it if he joined
my crew and came with us.

164
00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:44.000
But, it seems like he really wants to stay
here and cook with all of you guys.

165
00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.130
You can ask me all you want,
but I'm just not gonna take him.

166
00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:53.220
So you're saying you can't agree to it
until he tells you himself, s'that right?

167
00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.970
That's right! More food, please!

168
00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:57.680
Well, I suppose that's fair enough.

169
00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:02.480
But, who knows if that hardheaded little
brat will ever agree to join up with you.

170
00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:07.490
Yeah, once that guy makes up his mind,
there's nothin' anybody can do to change it.

171
00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:08.780
More, please!

172
00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:38.430
Sanji!

173
00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.430
What is that? A fishman?

174
00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:42.600
Did he come all the
way from the Fishman Islands

175
00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:43.940
– to eat here?
– You dolt!

176
00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:46.070
It's a human and a panshark!

177
00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:47.480
Huh? What's this?

178
00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.320
Whoa! It's Yosaku!

179
00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.820
Oh, hey... Big Bro Luffy.

180
00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:53.740
How come you're alone?
Where are the others?

181
00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:56.330
Did you find Nami?

182
00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:06.090
We never actually caught up to her,
but, from the direction Big Sis is headed,

183
00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:09.510
we think we've figured out where
she's going and what she plans to do.

184
00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:13.090
I see...
Then we can bring her back.

185
00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:15.090
Maybe... It's just...

186
00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.010
IF our suspicions turn out to be true,

187
00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.350
then the place she intends to
go could mean certain death

188
00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:21.180
for all of us, if we follow her.

189
00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.440
The point is, we really
need your help, Big Bro Luffy.

190
00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:26.980
Please! Come with me!

191
00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:31.070
Okay... I don't really get it,
but I got it. Let's go.

192
00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:42.160
Wait.

193
00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:43.660
Your dream is foolish.

194
00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.130
Then again, so's mine.

195
00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:50.670
Now is as good a time as any.

196
00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:53.840
Why not start my quest, right now?

197
00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.260
Sanji...

198
00:10:56.260 --> 00:11:00.600
I'll be joining your little crew,
on your journey to be King of the Pirates.

199
00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:03.560
You hear me?

200
00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:05.900
I want to be the cook on your ship.

201
00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:07.980
All right? What do you say?

202
00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.940
Yeah!

203
00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:11.230
Of course!

204
00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:13.110
This is great, Big Bro Luffy!

205
00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:13.780
Woo hoo!

206
00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:14.490
We got a cook!

207
00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:16.530
Now we'll get the tasty food!

208
00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.070
We got a cook!

209
00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:21.240
Are you guys happy now, or what?

210
00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.870
Sorry. Really, I'll leave now.

211
00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:25.660
Ha! I don't like it!

212
00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:28.170
To tell ya' the truth, I was
hopin' to give you the boot

213
00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:29.630
from this restaurant personally.

214
00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:34.130
But, it seems that you don't have
a problem with straight up abandoning us.

215
00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:38.090
I'm especially sorry for making
the lot of you resort to bad acting.

216
00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.850
Hey, wait! How'd you know?

217
00:11:39.850 --> 00:11:41.220
I heard everything!

218
00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.560
You bunch of jerks!

219
00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:44.060
What?!

220
00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:47.270
Was stomping on my pride the best
plan that you could come up with?

221
00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:48.270
Was it?

222
00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:50.020
You damn geezer.

223
00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:52.270
Every little thing has
to be a fight with you!

224
00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:53.730
Well, I'm sick and tired of it!

225
00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:55.740
Bring it on! Huh?

226
00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:59.240
Hmph. I never have liked children.

227
00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.950
As a matter of fact, I hate children.

228
00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:04.080
There wasn't a day passed
when I didn't regret

229
00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:06.580
letting a useless little
brat like you live, Sanji.

230
00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:10.330
Ha! Fine by me, you rotten old man.

231
00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:13.550
Enjoy the rest of your miserable life.

232
00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:15.210
Whoa! This is a nice ship!

233
00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.800
You sure it's okay to use her?

234
00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:19.510
Of course! It's Sanji's ship!

235
00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:21.720
You still need more?

236
00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.510
Yup! Gonna need more meat!

237
00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:26.520
All right, well how many days
are you gonna be out at sea?

238
00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:27.480
I don't know...

239
00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:34.070
It's the nicest sea
restaurant I've ever seen!

240
00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:35.940
That's for sure!

241
00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:42.070
<b>Baratie Employee Guidelines
1. Serving customers equals love,
and love equals restaurant!
2. Motto! Motto!
It's my service motto!
3. A pleasant greeting equals service!
4. The customer is king!</b>

242
00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:00.430
Hey, Sanji, listen...

243
00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:02.430
Hm? What is it?

244
00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:06.060
It doesn't matter what sort
of person walks through our doors.

245
00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:07.390
If they're hungry...

246
00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:10.100
Then they will be fed...

247
00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:14.770
Every starving wretch who comes
to us will get a fine meal.

248
00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:16.570
We can make that happen.

249
00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:20.610
It doesn't matter how much we fight,
because we share the same dream.

250
00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.910
Yeah!

251
00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:24.070
Are you ready?

252
00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:25.240
'Cause we're gonna be busy!

253
00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:28.620
You bet! It won't be
a problem with me around!

254
00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:39.010
Ow...

255
00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.140
Awful!

256
00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.100
Is that what you call peeling?!

257
